# One entry per accepted finding, each with why it is unreachable or blocked
# upstream and when to look again.

# gh 2.102.0 (the newest release when this was written) is built with Go
# 1.27.1 and golang.org/x/net 0.58.0. All three findings are denial of
# service in Go's HTTP and TLS code, per Trivy's titles:
#
#   HIGH  CVE-2026-78667  stdlib 1.27.1         DoS via crafted HTTP Range headers
#   HIGH  CVE-2026-78669  stdlib, x/net 0.58.0  DoS via excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS
#   HIGH  CVE-2026-97031  stdlib 1.27.1         DoS in crypto/tls via ECH outer extensions
#
# Not fixable here: the fix is a rebuild of gh on Go 1.27.2 / x/net 0.60.0,
# which is upstream's to ship. Nothing newer than 2.102.0 exists to move to.
#
# Limited reach: gh is a client run for one command at a time, never a
# listener, and this container's only route out is the gateway's allowlist.
# The worst case for each is one gh invocation that hangs or dies.
#
# Revisit: on every GH_VERSION bump. Remove an entry as soon as a gh release
# clears it; the scan fails again if a bump brings new findings.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
